const HELP_NEWS = "## 1.185.0 - 2026-11-19\n\n- Weekly review › Steps: Weekly review has its own item in the sidebar,\n  under Projects. It shows a number when the review is due. Hide it in\n  Settings › Sidebar if you do not want it (#450).\n\n## 1.184.2 - 2026-11-19\n\n- Your page: the GroupToDo logo now sits level with your picture at the\n  top of the sidebar, not lower down beside the text (#447).\n\n## 1.184.1 - 2026-11-19\n\n- The line menu and toolbar: what a long paste can become is offered right\n  under the pasted lines, in the page, not in the corner. It pushes the\n  lines below down rather than covering them, and stays through a redraw\n  (#449).\n\n## 1.184.0 - 2026-11-19\n\n- The line menu and toolbar: paste an email or a chat of 4 lines or more,\n  and the offer that appears has Plan it with an AI too. It opens the same\n  dialog as the line menu, with the pasted lines in the prompt, so a thread\n  becomes a project with one next action without picking the lines first\n  (#449).\n\n## 1.183.0 - 2026-11-19\n\n- Areas and sharing: a new area can go straight into a free serve.py\n  folder, as Server folder under Stored in. An area already in a server\n  folder can move to another free one. A browser area moving into a folder\n  that already holds pages asks first whether to bring its pages along. A\n  browser that cannot open folders is offered the server folder at the start\n  too (#432).\n\n## 1.182.2 - 2026-11-19\n\n- Journal: Back, Forward and Light or dark are back on a wide screen. They\n  went with the top bar; now Back and Forward stand at the left of the\n  day's heading, Light or dark at its right (#445).\n\n## 1.182.1 - 2026-11-19\n\n- The line menu and toolbar: To area is on the line menu too, as on the bar\n  under picked lines. It moves the line to another area (#443).\n\n## 1.182.0 - 2026-11-19\n\n- A page: drag a page pinned in the sidebar onto a line in the Journal or\n  on the page you are on, and a line linking it goes in below (#448). A bar\n  shows where it lands. Dropped on + New line, it goes last.\n\n## 1.181.0 - 2026-11-19\n\n- Your page: your picture now sits at the right of the sidebar's head, as\n  a button of its own that opens the page. The GroupToDo logo stands at the\n  left, with the version under the name; it opens What's new (#447).\n\n## 1.180.0 - 2026-11-19\n\n- Weekly review › Clarify: a new answer, Note for a responsibility, keeps\n  the line as a note and links the responsibility it is for (#437). A line\n  under one already is dealt at once. The To do answer now says you sort it\n  next, in Review actions (#438).\n- Weekly review › Actions: Not an action asks what it is instead: a\n  project, a note, or a note for a responsibility (#439). On a new day the\n  review starts again at Still to do, not in the pass you left it (#441).\n  Done already throws confetti, and every tenth one this week a big burst;\n  Celebration: off keeps it quiet (#442).\n- Journal: a day page lists the projects with its date in their title, or\n  on a line that links them, under Projects on this day (#440). Nothing is\n  written on the day.\n\n## 1.179.1 - 2026-11-19\n\n- Organisations › List: pages in a folder called O/, with a capital letter,\n  now move to o/ when the area opens, and every [[O/...]] link becomes\n  [[o/...]] (#434). So their names are offered again while you type. On\n  Windows and Android, where O/ and o/ are one folder, the move no longer\n  deletes the page it moved.\n\n## 1.179.0 - 2026-11-19\n\n- Present a page: a drawn slide (steps, pyramid, cycle, curve and the rest)\n  no longer shows its parts before they come (#433). Each part comes in on\n  its turn and stays, dimmed. A layout holds up to nine lines a slide, and\n  more are shared out evenly: ten is five and five, not nine and one. On a\n  page you have presented, or one with slide marks, the outline gives a red\n  bullet to each line past the fifth on a slide; pointing at it says why.\n";
